source: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/cloudflare/skills/main/skills/wrangler
vendored: 2026-08-16
split_of: SKILL.md
part: SKILL.md trim-tail 10
part: references/bindings-cli-reference.md trim-head 7

# Upstream ships one 922-line SKILL.md. We store the same bytes as two files,
# following this repo's references/ convention so a wrangler question does not
# drag 900 lines into context. Nothing of upstream is dropped:
#
#   upstream 1..281    == SKILL.md 1..281
#   upstream 282..922  == references/bindings-cli-reference.md 8..648
#
# The two trims are our own additions and nothing else — a 10-line pointer stub
# at the end of SKILL.md, and a 7-line header on the reference file.
#
# Because the layouts differ, refresh verifies this skill instead of fetching
# it: it reassembles the parts and compares them to upstream. Re-splitting is an
# editorial call, so when upstream changes the script reports and stops rather
# than guessing where to cut.
